def common_element(list1, list2):
    return any(item in list2 for item in list1)
```

This returns `True` on the first shared element and `False` otherwise. It returns an explicit `False` rather than falling through to `None`, so `assert common_element([1,2,3,4,5], [5,6,7,8,9]) == True` passes, and a no-match call returns `False`, not `None`.

